I decided my first attempt at improving the scoring system was
misguided and bad, and I have written a new patch to replace it. This
one is much simpler.

It places a limit on the score you can get from killing monsters,
eating tripe, and so on during the game. Once the game is over, the
usual calculations are performed for deepest level reached, gold,
artifacts, ascending, and all the rest.

The limit is 640000 points, which is what you would get if you reached
experience level 15 just by killing monsters. I think somebody said in
the scoring system thread that reaching level 15 without magic is
pretty much impossible, and that's how I picked this number. Feedback
would be very much appreciated.

-ML


